--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party tools
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project calls the ffmpeg command-line tools (ffmpeg, ffprobe) as external
processes. It does not bundle, link against, redistribute or modify them.
ffmpeg is a separate work by the FFmpeg project, licensed under the LGPL v2.1+
or GPL v2+ depending on how the build was configured:

    https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html

Install ffmpeg yourself. Nothing in this repository contains its code.

The optional `fer` extra, used only by the face-emotion backend, pulls in
opencv-python and tensorflow. Those are separate works under their own
licences, installed only if you ask for them. The default heuristic backend
requires none of them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Media
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository contains NO video, audio, image or model-weight files of any
kind. The sample footage used by the tests and by scripts/make_sample_footage.sh
is generated on demand with ffmpeg's own synthetic sources (testsrc2, smptebars,
sine, aevalsrc) and is deleted afterwards.

Your own footage is never copied into a project. A project stores file paths
and timecodes; only the finished film is written.
